- **Why `33` has higher contribution?** In model benchmarking, citations that support multiple baselines (e.g., `33` for Chi-Squared and Co-occurrence) are critical because they underpin more diverse evaluation metrics. This is common in AI/ML where a single citation can validate multiple aspects of model performance (e.g., statistical tests for Chi-Squared and co-occurrence analysis in NLP).
